A||||7||Jncomutt||Coupe Tail light Idea (thanx MinnGreen)||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||09-10-2001||06:45 PM||||Well.. I was thinking of the clear tailight assembly as MinnGreenGT had.  I don't have any special heat guns or what not so I decided on another idea.<P>As of now, I just stripped the black lines that run vertical and horizontal on the inner piece.  It looks cool, and much more clear without those little lines.  It wasn't complete tho.  Still had the red to deal with.  I stipped the black paint from those, and looked better yet.  Then when I had everything apart, I put the two clear lenses in one assembly together.  Looked Great!  It has that stock 'diffused' look from the original piece where the bulbs aren't too bright.  I use regular red glass bulbs to make them light.  The one thing that you will notice is that the curved part of the corner gets left open.  I cut the outside 3 blocks of the curved part from the red plastic and inserted that there for now.  I will have the pics up later this weekend.  Still looks good with that short red corner, plus add a darker red light at night.  Anyone have any opinions on this, or what I can interchange for the curved cornerpart?  <P>Btw, I used a spare set to work with.. I can still get back my originals if nothing comes up...||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||09-10-2001||11:26 PM||||Jncomutt-  sounds different... can't wait to see pics.  Monkeyman gave me a spare coupe light to mess with, so I'm going to try the diffuser lens on that to see what kind of results I get there.  Good luck- and thanks for the credit!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||09-11-2001||10:54 PM||||Guys...I just picked up some of the defuser stuff at Home Depot.  It is going to work perfect with no heating, cause the coupe style does not need it.  I just cut a piece to fit the area and now I am going to mask off the area and paint some flat black on the area that has no lights.  It looks great.  I just need to find the LED lights for more intence light.<P>Pics soon (When I fix my PIP)<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jncomutt||09-12-2001||12:29 AM||||I'm curious what you did for the edge?  There is certainly a slight bend there.  Is it too little for the plastic to need heat?  If its direct smooth fit like you say, I too will ditch the stock pieces.  Thanks GTA||||reg||1
Z||000004||b lo 0||09-12-2001||01:17 AM||||You know, funny thing is the same day MinnGreen posted the original idea, I had been thinking the same thing sitting in the break room at work.  But I got another idea.  Clear fixture stuff, and the white grid light cover stuff for the same style lights, with the grid painted black.  I think I'll try it.  I've also seen Acura's with taillights that are all red (brake, turn & reverse) and it looks great.  I may try butchered outer red lenses in the middle to see what it looks like.  I'll update...<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">       <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.vstoreauto.com.com" TARGET=_blank>Audio Imagery</A>, budget-priced car audio supplies from people like Monster Cable, Sony & more!||||reg||1
